  "body": "**Describe the bug**\n\nThe app-tile \"ping\" health check (`sendPingRequestAsync` / `withTimeoutAsync`) uses a fetch timeout that appears to be hardcoded internally, with no way to override it per-app or globally. Any monitored endpoint that legitimately takes longer than this to respond gets permanently flagged as \"down\" even though it is healthy.\n\n**Concrete example**\n\nA Nextcloud AIO mastercontainer admin interface (`https://<host>:8080`) consistently takes ~7-8 seconds to respond to a plain request (confirmed via direct curl, reproducible every time) due to its own internal orchestration checks. Homarr's ping check aborts before that, logging:\n\n```\nerror: Failed to send ping request url=\"https://<host>:8080\"\nAbortError: This operation was aborted\n```\n\n**Expected behavior**\n\nEither a configurable timeout (per-app field on the app/tile config, and/or a global server setting), or at minimum a longer default, so tiles pointing at slower-but-healthy admin backends do not get permanently reported as failing.\n\n**Environment**\n\n- Homarr (Docker), latest as of 2026-08.\n",
